<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. da Vinci is a 65-year-old man with ulnar neuropathy at the right elbow on splinting and hand therapy, and hypercholesterolemia on atorvastatin, who came in the same day with red eyes. Three days ago his right eye became red, gritty, and watery, and yesterday the left eye followed; the lids are crusted in the morning. A student in his studio had red eyes last week. He has had a slight sore throat. He has no eye pain, light sensitivity, blurred vision, halos, or discharge of thick pus, and he does not wear contact lenses. He rubs his eyes with his left hand while drawing. His hand is unchanged and he wears the night splint. He takes atorvastatin without muscle aches. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Onset</td><td>Three days; right eye first, then left</td></tr><tr><td>Associated signs and symptoms</td><td>Grittiness, watering, morning crusting, mild sore throat</td></tr><tr><td>Pertinent negatives</td><td>No pain, photophobia, reduced vision, or contact lens use</td></tr><tr><td>Exposure</td><td>A student with red eyes last week</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

